24:["$","section",null,{"style":{"padding":"var(--space-16) 0"},"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"reading-container","children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"2rem"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"var(--text-xs)","textTransform":"uppercase","letterSpacing":"0.05em","color":"var(--brand-primary)","fontWeight":700},"children":"Common Questions"}],["$","h2",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.4rem"},"children":"About the Platform"}]]}],["$","$L34",null,{"items":[{"id":"about-faq-0","title":"How is DevProjects different from typical college project idea lists?","content":"Generic listicles only give you a title and a short paragraph. Every DevProjects guide is structured as an engineering blueprint covering problem framing, system architecture diagrams, normalized database schemas, REST API specifications, step-by-step implementation snippets, and grouped placement interview questions."},{"id":"about-faq-1","title":"Who are these engineering project guides designed for?","content":"Our content is built primarily for B.Tech CSE, B.E. CSE/IT, BCA, and MCA students across India and globally—whether you are preparing a final-year degree capstone, building a backend or AI/ML centerpiece for campus placements, or completing a semester minor project."},{"id":"about-faq-2","title":"How do you review technical accuracy and prevent outdated code?","content":"Every project guide and editorial article follows an explicit authoring and peer-review lifecycle tracked with published, updated, and last-reviewed dates. Experienced systems architects and AI/ML practitioners verify schema constraints, concurrency patterns, and interview tradeoffs before publication."},{"id":"about-faq-3","title":"Can I extend these architectures for my own university submission or resume?","content":"Yes. Each guide intentionally explains architectural tradeoffs, extension ideas, and viva defense points so you can implement the core system cleanly, customize features for your evaluation rubric, and explain every design decision confidently in technical interviews."}]}]]}]}]}]
